<?xml version="1.0" encoding="ISO-8859-1"?>
<wps:ProcessDescriptions xmlns:wps="http://www.opengis.net/wps/1.0.0" xmlns:ows="http://www.opengis.net/ows/1.1" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.opengis.net/wps/1.0.0 schemas/wps/1.0.0/wpsDescribeProcess_response.xsd" service="WPS" version="1.0.0" xml:lang="en-US">
	<ProcessDescription wps:processVersion="1" storeSupported="true" statusSupported="false">
		<ows:Identifier>MiraMon:IMGIMG:1</ows:Identifier>
		<ows:Title>IMGIMG</ows:Title>
		<ows:Abstract><![CDATA[This program is used to compress and decompress raster files and for converting between IMG formats. For compressions/decompressions between IMG and JPEG formats use <a href="JPEGIMG.htm">JPEGIMG</a>. To decompress JPEG2000 formats (.jp2 or .j2c) please use <a href="J2KIMG.htm">J2KIMG</a>.]]></ows:Abstract>
		<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Title:Conversion of IMG files between MiraMon supported formats"/>
		<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Abstract:This program is used to compress and decompress raster files and for converting between IMG formats. For compressions/decompressions between IMG and JPEG formats use &lt;a href=&quot;JPEGIMG.htm&quot;&gt;JPEGIMG&lt;/a&gt;. To decompress JPEG2000 formats (.jp2 or .j2c) please use &lt;a href=&quot;J2KIMG.htm&quot;&gt;J2KIMG&lt;/a&gt;."/>
		<DataInputs>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>Opcio</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Option</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract><![CDATA[Option indicates the conversion and may be: <li>RLE to compress</li><li>UNRLE to decompress</li><li>a fixed format like: bit, byte, byte-RLE, integer, integer-RLE, uinteger, uinteger-RLE, long, long-RLE, real, real-RLE, bit-vell.</li><li>MINMAX to calculate the true minimum and maximum of the image and document it on the original image.</li>]]></ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param1"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:Option"/>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>RLE</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>UNRLE</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>bit</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>byte</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>byte-RLE</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>uinteger</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>uinteger-RLE</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>integer</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>integer-RLE</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>long</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>long-RLE</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>real</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>real-RLE</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>double</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>double-RLE</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>bit-vell</ows:Value>
						<ows:Value>MINMAX</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="1" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>FitxerOrigen</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Input file</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Is the file to convert.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param2"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:InputFile"/>
				<ComplexData>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-IMG</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-IMG</MimeType>
							<Encoding>Binary</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>MULTIBANDA</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Multiband</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Only applies for multiband rasters and indicates that all bands should be converted.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>RLE_INDEX</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Indexed RLE</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>When the result is a compressed raster setting this parameter will create a list of initial line positions at the end of the file.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#integer">integer</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>NO_EXTRA</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>No extracompression</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>When this parameter is set the compressed RLE format will use a lower compression than the usual extracompression.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AllowedValues>
						<ows:Value>##blank##</ows:Value>
					</ows:AllowedValues>
					<DefaultValue>##blank##</DefaultValue>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
			<Input minOccurs="0" maxOccurs="1">
				<ows:Identifier>MES_BANDA</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>One band</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>Name of the output file to add to the original multiband raster when the user only wishes to convert one of the original bands. Normally it is given without the path or the extension and it will be created in the same directory as the rest of the bands, but if the user wishes it can be any file name with any path.</ows:Abstract>
				<LiteralData>
					<ows:DataType ows:reference="http://www.w3.org/TR/xmlschema-2/#string">string</ows:DataType>
					<ows:AnyValue/>
				</LiteralData>
			</Input>
		</DataInputs>
		<ProcessOutputs>
			<Output>
				<ows:Identifier>Desti</ows:Identifier>
				<ows:Title>Output</ows:Title>
				<ows:Abstract>When the user does not wish to overwrite the original file, Output is the file containing the result of the conversion for single band images or the directory containing the result for multiband images for which all bands are to be converted.</ows:Abstract>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Param3"/>
				<ows:Metadata xlink:title="Name:Output"/>
				<ComplexOutput>
					<Default>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-IMG</MimeType>
							<Encoding>text</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Default>
					<Supported>
						<Format>
							<MimeType>application/x-IMG</MimeType>
							<Encoding>text</Encoding>
						</Format>
					</Supported>
				</ComplexOutput>
			</Output>
		</ProcessOutputs>
	</ProcessDescription>
</wps:ProcessDescriptions>